                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One reviewer said it best so I'm just going to borrow their words: [i]The story was far longer than it needed to be, due to heaps of filler content. For the most part, said content can be sorted into two categories: side stories that are meant to be funny but almost always end up being too tedious and dramatic; and condescending philosophical rants about how humans lie.[/i]\n\nI'll add that it could be fun if 1) the characters and scenes weren't [i]all[/i] written with the exact same humor and unseriousness, 2) the MC wasn't an insufferable jackass who takes nothing seriously unless it concerns him, and 3) there wasn't this exchange:\n\n\"I'm attracted to [a teenager in] the body of a little girl. Does that make me a monster?\n- Let's test it out. Imagine your ideal woman was blind. Would you still love her?\n- Yes.\n- What if half of her body was burnt? I'm sure you couldn't love her then!\"\n\nFirst of all, the MC is cruel for no reason once again. Second of all, why is there pedophilia in my quirky visual novel? Don't lampshade the loli if you can only make it worse. (also, the \"would you date X\" joke goes on for the rest of the game, but they literaly forget why it started. I can't be the only one haunted by the \"am I a pedophile\" memory??)\n\n[b]Cut 80% of it, stop trying to be funny all the time, and don't pretend there's a plot beside \"group of friends having fun in their last year of highschool\", and it'll be good. In it's current state though, it's not.[/b]\n\nOh, did I mention it \"ends\" with a guy being sexually harassed by his teacher (framed as \"haha ain't that the funniest thing ever\") while the MC thinks his worst monologue yet? [spoiler]The actual ending is a mess I won't talk about. It went \"wtf I hate this plot twist - wtf? - give my 4th wall back - the title is earned but why bother\". I won't talk about quality.[spoiler]",
